<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Drawing a quadratic using values from a table and using it to solve for the roots of x</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Draw the graph of \[ y = x^2 + {@p@}x + {@q@} \] for \({@xlo@} \le x \le {@xhi@}\), and use it to solve \(x^2 + {@p@}x + {@q@} =0\).</p>
<p><strong>a)</strong> Complete the table of values.</p>
<table border="1" cellpadding="6" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center">
<tr><th>\(x\)</th><td>\({@tx[1]@}\)</td><td>\({@tx[2]@}\)</td><td>\({@tx[3]@}\)</td><td>\({@tx[4]@}\)</td><td>\({@tx[5]@}\)</td><td>\({@tx[6]@}\)</td><td>\({@tx[7]@}\)</td></tr>
<tr><th>\(y\)</th><td>\({@ty[1]@}\)</td><td>[[input:ansY1]] [[validation:ansY1]]</td><td>[[input:ansY2]] [[validation:ansY2]]</td><td>\({@ty[4]@}\)</td><td>[[input:ansY3]] [[validation:ansY3]]</td><td>[[input:ansY4]] [[validation:ansY4]]</td><td>\({@ty[7]@}\)</td></tr>
</table>
<div>[[feedback:prtY1]] [[feedback:prtY2]] [[feedback:prtY3]] [[feedback:prtY4]]</div>
<p><strong>b)</strong> Plot the seven points from the table (drag each red point up or down to its \(y\)-value); a smooth curve is drawn through them.</p>
[[jsxgraph input-ref-ansP1="rP1" input-ref-ansP2="rP2" input-ref-ansP3="rP3" input-ref-ansP4="rP4" input-ref-ansP5="rP5" input-ref-ansP6="rP6" input-ref-ansP7="rP7" width="560px" height="540px"]]
var TX = {#tx#};
var PXLO={#float(pxlo)#}, PXHI={#float(pxhi)#}, PYLO={#float(pylo)#}, PYHI={#float(pyhi)#};
var brd = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox:[PXLO, PYHI, PXHI, PYLO], axis:true, grid:true, keepaspectratio:false, showCopyright:false, showNavigation:false});
var pts = [];
for (var i=0;i<7;i++){ pts[i] = brd.create('point',[TX[i],0],{name:'',color:'#cc0000',fillColor:'#cc0000',size:4,snapToGrid:true,snapSizeX:1,snapSizeY:1}); }
brd.create('curve', JXG.Math.Numerics.CardinalSpline(pts, 0.5), {strokeColor:'#1f4fd8', strokeWidth:2, highlight:false});
stack_jxg.bind_point(rP1, pts[0]);
stack_jxg.bind_point(rP2, pts[1]);
stack_jxg.bind_point(rP3, pts[2]);
stack_jxg.bind_point(rP4, pts[3]);
stack_jxg.bind_point(rP5, pts[4]);
stack_jxg.bind_point(rP6, pts[5]);
stack_jxg.bind_point(rP7, pts[6]);
[[/jsxgraph]]
<div style="display:none">[[input:ansP1]] [[validation:ansP1]] [[input:ansP2]] [[validation:ansP2]] [[input:ansP3]] [[validation:ansP3]] [[input:ansP4]] [[validation:ansP4]] [[input:ansP5]] [[validation:ansP5]] [[input:ansP6]] [[validation:ansP6]] [[input:ansP7]] [[validation:ansP7]]</div>
<div>[[feedback:prtPlot]]</div>
<p><strong>c)</strong> Solve for \(x^2 + {@p@}x + {@q@} =0\) using the graph.</p>
<div>\( x = \) [[input:ansR1]] [[validation:ansR1]] and \( x = \) [[input:ansR2]] [[validation:ansR2]] [[feedback:prtRoots]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>a)</strong> Substitute each \(x\) into \(y=x^2 + {@p@}x + {@q@} \). The completed table is:</p>
<table border="1" cellpadding="6" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center">
<tr><th>\(x\)</th><td>\({@tx[1]@}\)</td><td>\({@tx[2]@}\)</td><td>\({@tx[3]@}\)</td><td>\({@tx[4]@}\)</td><td>\({@tx[5]@}\)</td><td>\({@tx[6]@}\)</td><td>\({@tx[7]@}\)</td></tr>
<tr><th>\(y\)</th><td>\({@ty[1]@}\)</td><td>\({@ty[2]@}\)</td><td>\({@ty[3]@}\)</td><td>\({@ty[4]@}\)</td><td>\({@ty[5]@}\)</td><td>\({@ty[6]@}\)</td><td>\({@ty[7]@}\)</td></tr>
</table>
<p><strong>b)</strong> Plot the points and join them with a smooth parabola (shown below).</p>
<p><strong>c)</strong> The solutions of \(x^2 + {@p@}x + {@q@} =0\) are where the curve crosses the \(x\)-axis: \(x={@r1@}\) and \(x={@r2@}\).</p>
[[jsxgraph width="500px" height="480px"]]
var R1={#r1#}, R2={#r2#}, P={#p#}, Q={#q#};
var PXLO={#float(pxlo)#}, PXHI={#float(pxhi)#}, PYLO={#float(pylo)#}, PYHI={#float(pyhi)#};
var TX = {#tx#}, TY = {#ty#};
var brd = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox:[PXLO, PYHI, PXHI, PYLO], axis:true, grid:true, keepaspectratio:false, showCopyright:false, showNavigation:false});
brd.create('functiongraph',[function(x){ return x*x + P*x + Q; }, PXLO, PXHI],{strokeColor:'#1f4fd8', strokeWidth:2.5, highlight:false});
for (var i=0;i<7;i++){ brd.create('point',[TX[i],TY[i]],{name:'',fixed:true,color:'#000000',fillColor:'#000000',size:2}); }
brd.create('point',[R1,0],{name:'',fixed:true,color:'#cc0000',fillColor:'#cc0000',size:4});
brd.create('point',[R2,0],{name:'',fixed:true,color:'#cc0000',fillColor:'#cc0000',size:4});
[[/jsxgraph]]]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
